<description>&lt;p&gt;Ecuador is enforcing a fourth curfew through Nov. 10 in five coastal provinces as violence escalates, and the military has begun its first land operation against cartels with U.S. assistance, including U.S. Marines seizing a vessel linked to the Los Choneros gang in the eastern Pacific. Heavy rain on Santa Cruz Island in the Galapagos killed one person, left two missing, and a priest was killed when a crucifix fell on him, prompting an archbishop to announce a clergy safety plan. President Daniel Noboa continues to detain opposition leader Luisa González on money-laundering charges. The crisis recorded two battle-related deaths in 2019, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Amazon Frontlines&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijwFBVV95cUxQb2V4TUhQR2Q1RUVYeDFuM0ZBbEdYaEQycnJzV1BaSERUOEIxeXBZX25nQnNqUXpFcDc0dFNvLUNfVjJWVmMzczhkVmcxWFJaaWpXZkJ4WWFOLUNVMTVuUmt4a2hKQktyRVVidG9pTWctRmVuNlJjUExndVFndVBoTXF5cEpGOTgxejJPQk1KRQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;www.thetraveler.org&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikAFBVV95cUxPYVRJM2hjcFBjU0JDRm1JY1F0TEt2Z0VfYmNmRjRPVTVMWF9IZjY4WExxNDJ4YjFUcHo1OWFpR1JRU1hVaDNjdFJDZmZDdUIzY2k1WENlZUdyNWZid1I0dWtGMXpmNlVkblRRREoyd0lNT2ttekE0aldvSVJWSVVLVkRfckZDczBmSGQ1dEdrQmM?oc=5&quot;&gt;thetraveler.org&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Liverpool Echo&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipAFBVV95cUxOaFN5ZkJyNFhuSWRCTm5SLUp3NzlwWE80VDVOaWdrellTVW5IendaeHNiTFFVbXV3TDZsdTR1ZEVtY0pOVHczVWJRTFcwZ0dLQW5VSHBzblNUa2JjMXUya3JGQ0MxcF9Pek1vNFJNS19ubjNvU01nMVM2TVZNbnZHLW1hMk9DMnJHaHZoYXJxRXAxbi1YbTNObndQZ1YtaHVsTXZFYg?oc=5&quot;&gt;teleSUR English&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Korea Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;htt